<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Philip III Arrhidaeus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 359–317 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Philip III Arrhidaeus was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-macedon">Macedon</a> from 323 to 317 BCE, a son of Philip II and half-brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a>. Considered mentally impaired, he was proclaimed king after Alexander's death, jointly with Alexander's infant son Alexander IV, while real power lay with regents and generals. He was put to death in 317 BCE on the orders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/olympia">Olympias</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/philip-iii-arrhidaeus.jpg" alt="Philip III Arrhidaeus" width="320" height="153" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: LouisAragon · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gold_coin_of_Philip_III_Arrhidaios_struck_at_the_Babylon_mint_under_Archon,_Dokimos,_or_Seleukos_I.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The Argead line ended in the wars of the Diadochi: <b>Philip III Arrhidaeus</b> was executed by Olympias in 317 BCE and the boy Alexander IV put to death by Cassander in 311/310 BCE, and the Antipatrid and Antigonid dynasties held the throne until Rome abolished the monarchy in…</blockquote><a href="/empire/kingdom-of-macedon">Kingdom of Macedon · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>The Macedonian Empire fragmented almost immediately after Alexander's death at Babylon in 323 BCE, owing to the absence of a clear succession plan and the weakness of his heirs, his half-brother <b>Philip III Arrhidaeus</b> and his infant son Alexander IV.</blockquote><a href="/empire/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li></ul></section>
